    "q": "<p>Langbar Ltd grants 250 SARs to each of its 500 employees on 1 October 20X1 on the condition that the employees remain with the company for two years until 30 September 20X3. The SARs may be exercised after this date.</p><p>What expense is recognised in the year ended 31 December 20X3?</p><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><span>£776,400</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><span>£771,478</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><span>£593,400</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><span>£591,348</span></div>",
    "a": "<p class=\"answer-key\">The correct answer is b.</p><p>31 December 20X1</p><p>The total expected cost is £980,000 (250 x (500 - 3 - 7) x £8)</p><p>The expense in the year is £122,500 (£980,000 x 3/24 months)</p><p>31 December 20X2</p><p>The total expected cost is £1,288,875 (250 x (500 - 5 - 4) x £10.50)</p><p>The cumulative expense to date is £805,547 (£1,288,875 x 15/24 months)</p><p>The expense in the year is £683,047 (£805,547 - £122,500)</p><p>30 September 20X3</p><p>The total cost is £1,577,025 (250 x (500 - 11) x £12.90)</p><p>The expense in the year is £771,478 (£1,577,025 - £805,547)</p>",
