    "provider": "ICAS",
    "q": "<p>Skipton Ltd (Skipton) grants 400 SARs to each of its 100 employees on 1 January 20X6 on the condition that the employees remain with the company for four years until 31 December 20X9. The SARs may be exercised after this date.</p><p>Fair values of a SAR are £4 at 1 January 20X6, £6.50 at 31 December 20X6 and £9.50 at 31 December 20X7.</p><p>Five employees left the company in 20X6 and a further six were expected to leave before the vesting date as at 31 December 20X6. A further four did leave in 20X7 and another three were expected to leave before the vesting date as at 31 December 20X7.</p><p>Skipton pays tax at 20%.</p><p>What credit entry is made to profit or loss in the year ended 31 December 20X7 in respect of deferred tax on the SARs?</p><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">a)</span><span>£21,870</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">b)</span><span>£33,440</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">c)</span><span>£109,350</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><span class=\"choice-letter\">d)</span><span>£155,630</span></div>",
    "a": "<p>The correct answer is a.</p><p>The total expected cost of the SARs at 31 December 20X7 is £334,400 (400 x (100 - 5 - 4 - 3) x £9.50)</p><p>The cumulative cost to date (and the liability) at 31 December 20X7 is £167,200 (£334,400 x 2/4 years)</p><p>A deductible temporary difference (equal to the liability) gives rise to a deferred tax asset of £33,440 (20% x £167,200)</p><p>This is an increase to the asset of £21,870 (£33,440 - £11,570)</p><p>This is recognised by:</p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"accounting-table rebuilt-table\"><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\"></th><th scope=\"col\">Account name</th><th scope=\"col\">£</th><th scope=\"col\">£</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Dr</th><td class=\"num\">Deferred tax asset</td><td class=\"num\">21,870</td><td class=\"num\"></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Cr</th><td class=\"num\">Income tax expense (SPL)</td><td class=\"num\"></td><td class=\"num\">21,870</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Being the increase in the deferred tax asset.</p>",
    "isHTML": true,
    "linkTags": [
      "share-based-payments-disclosures"
    ]
